regelverk.org is an open database that collects regulations for different areas in one place, with clear sources, requirements and guidance.

The database is built around structured records – legislation, standards, frameworks, authorities, requirements, management systems and sectors – with metadata about status, issuer, jurisdiction and latest review. Each area has its own site, for example ot.regelverk.org for OT security and brandskydd.regelverk.org for fire safety.

regelverk.org is created and maintained by [Vincent Barkman](https://vincentbarkman.com). The source code is open under AGPL-3.0 and available on [GitHub](https://github.com/VincentBarkman/regelverk.org), where you are welcome to open an issue if you find an error or a regulation is missing.
